# Vapi Studio best practices (from `@guidify-ai/vapi-studio`)

This file is **managed by** `@guidify-ai/vapi-studio` `postinstall` (`scripts/install-agent-refs.cjs`). Do not replace it with app-specific rules — put those in a separate `.mdc`.

## Before you change conversation behavior

Read the framework guides (prefer the installed package path):

- `node_modules/@guidify-ai/vapi-studio/docs/best-practices/README.md`
- `node_modules/@guidify-ai/vapi-studio/docs/best-practices/conversation-design.md`
- `node_modules/@guidify-ai/vapi-studio/docs/best-practices/nodes-and-listens.md`
- `node_modules/@guidify-ai/vapi-studio/docs/best-practices/identity-and-pii.md`
- `node_modules/@guidify-ai/vapi-studio/docs/best-practices/debugging-and-observability.md`
- `node_modules/@guidify-ai/vapi-studio/docs/best-practices/documentation-layers.md`

Source checkout fallback: `docs/best-practices/` in the vapi-studio repository.

Also see `node_modules/@guidify-ai/vapi-studio/agent/AGENTS.md`.

## Non-negotiables

1. **One CTA per turn** — split stacked questions into more agent steps or `continueTo` hops.
2. **Constrained extracts fail closed** — e.g. NA mobile exactly 10 digits; never keep trailing ASR junk as PII.
3. **Listen timeout matches the answer** — short windows for digit collection.
4. **Logs/events explain every turn** — `ROUTE_DECISION`, memory flags, raw+normalized constrained fields; see debugging-and-observability guide.
5. **App README = northern stars only** — no flow dumps; doctrine lives in the guides above; runtime contracts in the package README.
